**Example Patent-Style Claim**

1. A wearable electronic device comprising:  
   a display configured to present payment-related information;  
   a touch-sensitive input surface configured to detect a touch input;  
   one or more processors; and  
   a memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the wearable electronic device to:  
   determine that an area or a pressure of the touch input exceeds a predetermined threshold;  
   in response to the determination, display an indicator identifying a selected item of the payment-related information;  
   detect a subsequent user input associated with the selected item; and  
   in response to the subsequent user input, display an enlarged representation of the selected item.
